{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Until your brother seeks it.</b> Now would it enter your mind that he would give it back to him before he seeks it? Rather — seek it out, so that you not be a deceiver (Bava Metzia 27; see Sifrei)." "<b>And you shall return it to him.</b> That there be in it a returning — that it not eat in your house toward its value, and you would then claim it from him. From here they said: anything that does work and eats — let it do work and eat; and that does not do work and eats — let it be sold (Bava Metzia 28)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:56.509257043Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}